[38;2;124;124;124mActually, the Jech-Sochor theorem (as stated in Jech's "The Axiom of Choice") [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msays: if a statement φ is consistent with ZFA + ¬AC and φ is boundable (i.e., φ [0m[38;2;124;124;124m↔ ∃S ψ(S) where ψ is a bounded formula - all quantifiers are bounded by TC(S)), [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthen φ is consistent with ZF.[0m

